<div class="container mkt-prose">
  <p>True North Outfitters opened in 1987 as a 400-square-foot shop in Toronto selling wool sweaters, work jackets and not much else. The bet was simple: carry clothes made by small North American makers, stand behind everything we sell, and treat every customer the way a good neighbour would.</p>

  <p>Thirty-nine years later the bet hasn't changed. We now partner with more than twenty independent brands &mdash; from <strong>Meridian Wool Co.</strong> in Nova Scotia to <strong>Kootenay Works</strong> in the BC interior &mdash; and operate over a hundred stores from St. John's to San Diego. We're still family-owned. Nobody has ever successfully explained "synergy" to our founder.</p>

  <h2>What we stand behind</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Made to keep.</strong> We'd rather sell you one jacket that lasts a decade than three that last a season. Free repairs on house-brand outerwear, forever.</li>
    <li><strong>Fair to makers.</strong> Every partner brand is audited for wages and working conditions. Most are small enough that we just visit.</li>
    <li><strong>Easy to deal with.</strong> 30-day returns, in any store or by mail, no interrogation.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The numbers</h2>
  <div class="about-stats">
    <div class="about-stat"><strong>1987</strong><span>Founded in Toronto</span></div>
    <div class="about-stat"><strong>100+</strong><span>Stores in 2 countries</span></div>
    <div class="about-stat"><strong>20+</strong><span>Independent brand partners</span></div>
    <div class="about-stat"><strong>2,400</strong><span>Employees &mdash; and counting</span></div>
  </div>

  <div class="mkt-cta-band">
    <h2>Come say hi.</h2>
    <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/stores">Find Your Store</a>
  </div>
</div>

